Z||000001||87GTZ34||09-12-2001||04:11 PM||||What does it take to start it again?  ie. a jump start, let it cool, replace the battery what.  This will help to diagnose the problem||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||09-12-2001||04:18 PM||||Leave an extra vehicle at point B   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Might want to inspect the connections at the starter.  Apparently they have been known to get loose from vibration.  If that's it, don't forget to disconnect the battery before you go to tighten the connections!  <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 09-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfixit58||09-12-2001||04:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87GTZ34:<BR><B>What does it take to start it again?  ie. a jump start, let it cool, replace the battery what.  This will help to diagnose the problem</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Agreed. If your not specific enough it's kinda like target shooting with a shotgun. If you get enough shot in the air, eventually you may get lucky and hit it.<P>But in the meantime, you may want to check and make sure the ignition switch is not loose. It's the silver and white thing mounted at the bottom of your steering column. The one with all the wires. It's rare but these can also go bad.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||1
