Z||000010||87GTZ34||09-13-2001||11:13 AM||||It may be the starter or the solenoid.  It is suffering from 'heat soak' which is exactly what it sounds like, heat is soaking into the starter components most likely after you shut the car down and no air is moving down there.  If the starter is shot you'll here the solenoid 'kick' and any electrical items (fans,lights fuel pump) will stop or dim/go out when trying to crank the car.  If it is the solenoid then the car typically won't even click when the key is turned.  GL and keep us posted on your findings.||||reg||1
